# followup-formula-utf16: representation and shared prerequisites

## Value/API contract

Value gains Utf16(Vec<u16>) for strings with isolated surrogate code units.
Construct through Value::from_utf16(Vec<u16>): well-formed input becomes the
existing Text(String), including when a concatenation repairs a surrogate pair.
Do not construct Utf16 for ordinary strings. No sentinel encoding is used.

Value::is_text() recognizes both variants; text_units() returns Option<Vec<u16>>.
Value::text_to_utf8_lossy() is an EXPLICIT final Buffer.from(str,"utf8") boundary.
It must not be used for slicing, joining, comparison or other intermediate values.

Public coerce helpers:
- to_js_utf16(&Value) -> Vec<u16>: lossless String(value), including array joining.
- utf16_number(&[u16]) -> f64, parse_float_utf16(&[u16]) -> f64,
  parse_int_utf16(&[u16], f64) -> f64: original numeric coercion/prefix behavior.
- case_utf16(&[u16], bool) -> Vec<u16>: scalar case conversion preserving isolated units.
Existing parse_string returns a Text or Utf16 value as needed.
Existing to_js_string remains an UTF-8-only adapter and asserts that its input is
well-formed; raw-aware consumers MUST use to_js_utf16. This prevents hidden U+FFFD
replacement. All reachable internal raw paths in the registered library were
migrated or delegated to the shared APIs below. Future function-library tasks
must add Utf16 to exhaustive matches and treat both variants as JS strings.

No functions/mod.rs, workspace manifest or dependency file was changed. token.rs
still accepts &str formula source; generated internal strings and Context values
can now carry raw UTF-16. A separate raw formula-source API is not introduced.

## Required root-owned shared bridge APIs (not implemented by this leaf)

    mixdog_js::regex_is_match_utf16(pattern: &[u16], text: &[u16], flags: &str)
        -> Result<bool, String>
    mixdog_js::locale_compare_utf16(a: &[u16], b: &[u16]) -> std::cmp::Ordering
    mixdog_js::time::date_parse_utf16(text: &[u16]) -> f64

The leaf now calls these exact signatures: there are NO temporary unsupported
refusals, UTF-8 replacement fallbacks or fabricated answers for these paths.
Compilation is blocked until the bridges land.

Regex: cached regress 0.10.5 supplies Regex::from_unicode(iterator<u32>, flags)
and, with feature "utf16", find_from_utf16(&[u16], start). Root owns enabling
that feature and retaining the shared JsRegex/V8 error-message contract. MATCH
performs the original pattern transformations over units before calling the API.
Do not convert pattern/input through String::from_utf16_lossy or sentinel chars.

Collation: IMPORTANT, cached icu_collator 2.4.0 compare_utf16 explicitly replaces
unpaired surrogates with U+FFFD, so simply exposing that method is NOT sufficient.
Node reports D800 < D801 < FFFD through localeCompare. The new VLOOKUP fixture
exercises this distinction. A surrogate-preserving implementation is required;
no implementation is claimed here. Existing default-locale semantics must remain.

Date parsing: the existing mixdog-js date_parser already has Reader.units:Vec<u16>.
Expose that path rather than sanitizing to UTF-8. Original Node accepts, for
example, a raw D800 before " Jan 1, 2024" or inside a trailing parenthesized
comment. Returning #VALUE for all raw date text is incorrect; fixtures cover it.
This is parsing, separate from locale-dependent Date display names.

## Implemented paths

CHAR/UNICHAR, LEFT/RIGHT/MID, CLEAN, CODE/UNICODE, CONCAT/CONCATENATE and engine &,
TEXTJOIN, REPT, REPLACE/SUBSTITUTE, FIND/SEARCH, LOWER/UPPER/TRIM/PROPER, EXACT/LEN,
NUMBERVALUE/VALUE/T, numeric format token scans, JS equality/relational predicates,
TYPE/ISTEXT/ISNONTEXT, logical string handling, SUM numeric-prefix behavior,
array-to-string, criteria literals, database addition/comparison, lookup indexing,
string iteration, raw regex/locale dispatch and date parsing dispatch preserve units.
Statistical direct_array and array_length changes were explicitly authorized by root.

The original coerce::date_to_string implementation was retained unchanged. The four
locale/timezone-display cases remain the separate followup-date-display prerequisite.
No NaN or surrogate comparison normalization was introduced.

## Exception text boundary (remaining exact-output limitation)

Failure::Thrown(String) was NOT expanded, as instructed. SERIESSUM/INTERCEPT
TypeError messages containing an input's raw units become well-formed only at
that explicit final UTF-8 error boundary. Internal argument values stay intact.
The reference recording includes both JSON bytes and direct UTF-8 bytes of such
a message. They differ: JSON.stringify preserves \ud800 as an escape, whereas
Buffer.from(message,"utf8") replaces it. Preserved original ext-host at
commit d47494aa5fd9662170425a26adc3498a19dd658d (worker-core.mjs/frame.mjs) sends
Buffer.from(JSON.stringify(frame)), so the raw difference survives that transport.
Final model/UI handling beyond this frame was not examined. This is an explicit
remaining error-output limitation, not a claim of full raw exception-message parity.
No arbitrary Failure variant/API change was made to hide or bypass it.

## Evidence and gates

Node recorder: tests/record-utf16.mjs, against C:/Project/mixdog read-only.
Fixture: tests/utf16-reference.json, 28 formulas + 19 direct-library cases.
Fixture SHA-256: ad535626f2eee394ea106347f60a4e3009381f3263907b7984adbfd55184a34d
Test: tests/twin_utf16.rs compares raw units, numeric bits and explicit UTF8/XML
bytes. It includes raw MATCH, locale VLOOKUP and DATEVALUE, with no ignored cases.
The existing twin_text_date encoder now exposes raw units and separately verifies
all eight recorded engine XML-unit and XML-UTF8 outputs, previously not replayed.
Other exhaustive twin encoders were extended without changing expected fixtures.

No Rust compile/test/build, app run, dependency download or commit was performed.
rustfmt parsed/formatted the changed sources. After shared bridges land, root
must run strict twin_math (4285), twin_stats_descriptive (3226), twin_engine,
twin_text_date and twin_utf16. The prior 15 differences are not declared resolved
until that execution; the Date-display four are explicitly still separate.
Root must adapt actual workbook writers to the explicit final UTF-8 boundary;
these tests demonstrate the conversion, not an already-wired ZIP writer.
